  "case_reason": "The counterexample 'Six' relies on the premise that six is an even integer but not divisible by four. This premise is factually true (6 % 2 == 0, 6 % 4 != 0). However, the literal assertion contains a universal quantifier ('even integers --[are divisible by]--> four'), which implies 'for all even integers x, x is divisible by 4'. The counterexample provides a specific instance where the condition (being an even integer) holds but the consequence (divisibility by four) fails. Therefore, the case successfully refutes the universal claim.",
